1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,378
Starting in 1928, thousands of people

2
00:00:03,388 --> 00:00:05,743
stood on an Indiana sand dune to watch

3
00:00:05,753 --> 00:00:08,479
skiers fly off a tower nearly 200 feet

4
00:00:08,489 --> 00:00:08,788
tall.

5
00:00:09,338 --> 00:00:10,614
You asked for Portage.

6
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:13,204
This was right next door, in Ogden Dunes.

7
00:00:13,654 --> 00:00:16,841
The jump was built in 1927 for what became

8
00:00:16,851 --> 00:00:18,362
the Ogden Dunes Ski Club.

9
00:00:18,592 --> 00:00:20,888
A state marker calls it reputedly the

10
00:00:20,898 --> 00:00:23,254
largest artificial ski jump of its day.

11
00:00:23,704 --> 00:00:25,880
For five winters, skiers from other

12
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:28,399
countries competed here, and crowds of

13
00:00:28,409 --> 00:00:30,801
7,000 to 20,000 came to watch.

14
00:00:31,251 --> 00:00:33,033
Then came the Great Depression, and

15
00:00:33,043 --> 00:00:34,253
winters with little snow.

16
00:00:34,803 --> 00:00:35,769
The meets ended.

17
00:00:35,999 --> 00:00:37,907
The tower was sold to a ski club in

18
00:00:37,917 --> 00:00:39,961
Rockford, Illinois, and taken down.

19
00:00:40,611 --> 00:00:43,318
Today, a state historical marker in Ogden

20
00:00:43,328 --> 00:00:44,563
Dunes tells the story.

21
00:00:44,793 --> 00:00:46,570
Please respect private property.

22
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:49,063
Comment your town, and it could be next.

